# Asserted test-count floors — ONE definition, sourced by every gate.
#
# These scripts assert the COUNT, not the exit code, because a runner whose glob
# matches nothing exits 0 having run zero tests. That design only works if the
# numbers are right, and they had drifted: the same Kotlin floor was written in
# two places (one as a hand-summed total), and the appd floor was >0 in the script
# that puts the DAEMON into production while the desktop release demanded >=300 —
# so the production path accepted a suite that had lost 90% of its tests.
#
# Raise a floor here when tests are added; never edit a copy in a script.

KOTLIN_SHARED_MIN=947    # :core jvm + :core android + :app + :ui jvm   (actual 952 on 2026-08-26)
#
# Raised on 2026-08-26 by the plan/usage rework: the countdown, the RFC 3339
# parse, the minor-unit money and the extra-usage state line moved into :core as
# PlanFormat, so their 29 tests run on BOTH targets and count twice. They are
# there because the two shells had been answering the same questions differently
# — one of them with the timezone offset sliced off the timestamp.
#
# Raised again on 2026-08-26 by Rounds polish: HuginnClient.polishRound pins the
# whole draft reaching the wire, the poll tier the call rides, and the one that
# matters most — a degraded 200 {error} decoding as an ERROR rather than throwing.
# Three tests in :core's commonTest, so they run on both targets and count twice.
#
# Raised again on 2026-08-26 by device lifecycle: agoWordsMs (:core commonTest, so
# it counts on both targets) and the "not reachable · last seen 3 days ago" line in
# the shared DevicesView — seven cases in :ui, most of them about what must NOT be
# rendered, because a bare "last seen" or a 1970 stamp is worse than no clause.
DESKTOP_EXTRA_MIN=203    # + :app-desktop, added on top of the shared floor (actual 208 on 2026-08-26)
#
# Was 189 from the day these floors were consolidated, which was ALWAYS above the
# real count — this file's own header says the numbers had drifted and one was a
# hand-summed total, and 189 was the hand-summed one. Checked 2026-08-23: no
# :app-desktop test file has been deleted since, and 14 remain, so nothing was
# lost; the number was simply never true. It never fired because the assertion is
# on the SUM (KOTLIN_SHARED_MIN + DESKTOP_EXTRA_MIN), which the shared half kept
# clearing on its own — a floor that cannot fail is not a floor.
#
# Raised on 2026-08-26 by device lifecycle: the "actual 177" above was already
# stale (the suite had reached 186 before this change), and 22 more arrived with
# it — Unenrol's whole state machine, which is where "keep the handle until the
# DELETE lands" is actually decided, plus the settings half that records the debt
# and survives a laptop being closed before the daemon could be told.
APPD_MIN=709             # server/appd node --test  (actual 713 on 2026-08-26)
#
# Raised on 2026-08-26 with the plan fixture: the 2026-07-27 capture was replaced
# by a live one whose extra usage is switched OFF while $100.55 of it is spent,
# and the new cases pin both halves of that — the gate that now shows it, and the
# never-enabled account that must still show nothing.
#
# Raised again on 2026-08-26 by Rounds polish: lib/polish (23) covers the runtime
# frame the polish prompt teaches and the distrustful parse around the answer, and
# routes-polish (15) covers the endpoint — including the CAGE itself, asserted off
# the argv a stub claude records, because `--tools ""` and `--setting-sources ""`
# going missing changes nothing anyone could see in a reply.
#
# Raised again on 2026-08-26 by device lifecycle: 19 covering the uninstall sweep
# and the registry on disk. The load-bearing ones are the negatives — that an
# outage mid-sweep is never read as a dead token (it would empty the registry in
# one pass, with no way back but reinstalling on every phone), and that
# `validate_only` sits BESIDE the message rather than inside it, where it would
# turn a daily probe into a real 3am push to every device.
